es the new value and may return a Promise. Use it for settings that are saved through an API as soon as they change, such as enabling an account or notifications.",[334,346],{"name":347},"switch-action",[349,350,351,374],"table",{},[352,353,354],"thead",{},[355,356,357,361,363,368],"tr",{},[358,359,360],"th",{},"Stage",[358,362,152],{},[358,364,365],{},[291,366,367],{},"v-model",[358,369,370,373],{},[291,371,372],{},"change"," event",[375,376,377,392,406,418],"tbody",{},[355,378,379,383,386,389],{},[380,381,382],"td",{},"Pending",[380,384,385],{},"Shows the new value, loading and disabled",[380,387,388],{},"Unchanged",[380,390,391],{},"Not emitted",[355,393,394,397,400,403],{},[380,395,396],{},"Success",[380,398,399],{},"Keeps the new value, loading and disabled end",[380,401,402],{},"Updated to the new value",[380,404,405],{},"Emitted",[355,407,408,411,414,416],{},[380,409,410],{},"Failure",[380,412,413],{},"Goes back to the old value, loading and disabled end",[380,415,388],{},[380,417,391],{},[355,419,420,423,426,428],{},[380,421,422],{},"Error",[380,424,425],{},"Same as failure",[380,427,388],{},[380,429,391],{},[431,432,433,450,467,475],"ul",{},[434,435,436,439,440,443,444,446,447,302],"li",{},[437,438,396],"strong",{},": only returning ",[291,441,442],{},"false"," (or a Promise resolving to ",[291,445,442],{},") counts as a failure. Any other value is a success, including no return value as in ",[291,448,449],{},"async () => { await save(value) }",[434,451,452,455,456,459,460,463,464,466],{},[437,453,454],{},"Errors",": when the action throws, the switch reverts the same way and the error is thrown again, for the global error handler or the console. To notify the user, ",[291,457,458],{},"try","\u002F",[291,461,462],{},"catch"," inside the action, show a message and return ",[291,465,442],{},", as in the example above.",[434,468,469,471,472,474],{},[437,470,382],{},": the switch is disabled, so the action is not called twice. If the page changes ",[291,473,367],{}," while pending, the page's value wins and is not overwritten when the action finishes.",[434,476,477,482,483,485,486,302],{},[437,478,479,480],{},"Without ",[291,481,297],{},", ",[291,484,367],{}," updates right after toggling, the same as ",[291,487,301],{},[288,489,490,491,494,495,498,499,302],{},"The ",[291,492,493],{},"SwitchAction"," and ",[291,496,497],{},"SwitchValue"," types can be imported from ",[291,500,501],{},"#shuo-ui\u002Fcomponents\u002FShuoSwitch.vue",[309,503,505],{"id":504},"on-and-off-values","On and off values",[288,507,508,494,511,514,515,494,518,520,521,459,524,527],{},[291,509,510],{},"true-value",[291,512,513],{},"false-value"," are the bound values when on and off, ",[291,516,517],{},"true",[291,519,442],{}," by default. Change them when the back end uses ",[291,522,523],{},"Y",[291,525,526],{},"N","; the action receives these values too.",[334,529],{"name":530},"switch-values",[309,532,534],{"id":533},"size-and-states","Size and states",[288,536,537,538,541,542,545,546,549,550,553,554,557,558,561,562,565,566,569,570,574],{},"When ",[291,539,540],{},"size"," is not set, it follows the ",[291,543,544],{},"UFormField"," size and the site-wide setting, ",[291,547,548],{},"lg"," built in, the same as the other input components. Without a description, the switch height matches an input of the same size (24 to 40px for ",[291,551,552],{},"xs"," to ",[291,555,556],{},"xl","), so it lines up with other fields in the same row. ",[291,559,560],{},"loading"," shows a loading icon and disables the switch; ",[291,563,564],{},"disabled"," follows the form state when not set; ",[291,567,568],{},"skeleton"," covers it with a skeleton of the same size. See ",[324,571,573],{"href":572},"\u002Fcomponents\u002Foverview\u002Fcommon","Common props"," for the shared behavior of the states.",[334,576],{"name":577},"switch-states",[288,579,580,482,582,494,585,588,589,592,593,302],{},[291,581,540],{},[291,583,584],{},"color",[291,586,587],{},"loadingIcon"," ca